{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/633647-2ed-mesmerized-iron-edict","id":633647,"title":"[2ed] Mesmerized & Iron Edict","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-20T12:12:27-07:00","id":633647,"title":"[2ed] Mesmerized & Iron Edict","content":"Hi all please help me with this doubt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> A player during a combat against another vampire used mesmerize giving the command: &quot;Flee&quot;. He achieved more successes in the contested roll so the power worked. The question is: How long the vampire should flee? How many turns? And if he give the command &quot;Sleep&quot; ?<br /> Only by hypothesis using iron edict in the same situation giving a more complex command, how would it work? For example saing: &quot;run up to your haven and put yourself to sleep&quot;.<br /> Using a more complex sentence, that requires more then one turn to say, the enemy stops to attacks and lose all his actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-20-2015, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:05:46-07:00","id":633726,"title":"","content":"Mostly, these are answered by the relevant Conditions. The specifics is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Mesmerized: If you define &quot;fleeing&quot; as &quot;escaping combat&quot; then they could flee until they've escaped combat then stop. Elsewise you could have it keep going until Mesmerize is broken.<br /> Dominated: This explicitly says it lasts until the command comes to a natural end or at sunrise if there is no natural end.<br /> <br /> Do note that doing it in combat is only really helpful on the defensive, like the examples you posted. Taking damage and a few other things break Dominate, so it's not really practical in combat. It also requires eye contact, so I wouldn't begrudge any Storyteller that said you can't use it in combat at all, or you have to make a roll to establish eye contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:16:43-07:00","id":633735,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Yes I know it should be used just to escape form a fight that is going bad. Regarding the eyes contact, the book says that a second is enough to establish the mesmerize condition...it's not so weird see the eyes of an enemy unless it is tring to avoid them actively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:50:51-07:00","id":633762,"title":"","content":"Note that unless you score an Exceptional Success you cannot give an order the same turn you inflicted the Mesmerized Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T17:05:45-07:00","id":634016,"title":"","content":"In a CWoD game, we had a houserule regarding a &quot;sleep&quot; command; the target will not immediately lose consciousness, but will go find someplace safe and relatively comfortable to take a nap. A vampire will not sleep outdoors, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T17:49:08-07:00","id":634075,"title":"","content":"Yes but probably there is difference between the command: &quot;go to sleep&quot; and &quot;fall asleep&quot; or even &quot;faint&quot;. The second and third ones could be the common vampire's power seen in the most part of films, with wich she let the victim unconscious.<br /> I remember that in masquerade was written that during combat that kind of command persist only for a turn. But in second edition of requiem there isn't a specification for using it during combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T18:35:28-07:00","id":634142,"title":"","content":"I would say that if you ordered someone to sleep using Dominate they would just lay down and attempt to go to sleep. I probably wouldn't have them just instantly fall asleep because most people can't really do that. They would try to fall asleep to the best of their ability, but depending on the person that could take anywhere from a few seconds after laying down to hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:59:53-07:00","id":634859,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashenrogue</b> have an important point. Dominate doesn't affect the targets ability to carry out the command. It ISN'T the power of making the victim faint (though it could be a Devotion). A victim of Dominate will try her best to faint if ordered to, but she isn't more able to just faint now than she was without Dominate. I can't do that, at least. I barely can sleep in less than 10 minutes at my own bed. I would rule that a character like myself would just try to survive combat (since I can't sleep if dead, and I won't count eternal slumber as the same, thank you) and look for a quiet place with actual chance of sleeping, since the command makes me do it at my best, and my best says that I just WON'T sleep at a cold street in the middle of a fight, unless I went two days in a roll without sleep. A vampire target would simply ignore it for the moment, since she can't even sleep at night unless torpid.<br /> <br /> Other relevant tip: though mesmerize takes only a second, the Eye Contact rule is still there to control abuse. People doesn't look in the eyes so much for nothing. Certainly during an intense fight there can be a moment where the combatants lock eyes, but most of the time not. The idea is to hold the target attention on your eyes for a moment, not on your body language (the top priority during a fight). It seems too much for me to use Mesmerize in the heat of battle without something to actually attract the target's attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:24:33-07:00","id":634874,"title":"","content":"Well, &quot;Sleep&quot; was a good one-word command back in 1e. In 2e, without the one-word restriction, you can just say &quot;Don't move!&quot; for an equivalent effect; you can rewrite their memory anyways, so not like them seeing something is important. So, the whole &quot;fall asleep where you stand&quot; is merely one of aesetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}